      "description": "A suspension or self-leveling warning on a G05 X5 is not proof that its compressor, air struts, or springs failed. Equipment differs by VIN, and BMW has documented narrowly defined causes including incorrectly secured rear ride-height-sensor control rods on affected vehicles, a software-only 80422D fault on a limited production range without the air-suspension options, and an air-line installation issue on a small set of 2026 vehicles. The earlier article incorrectly combined E70, F15, and G05 systems, presented failures as inevitable at a fixed mileage, and recommended generic compressor and coil-conversion products without identifying the failed component or exact application.",
      "solution": "Start with the VIN build/options, open-campaign status, exact warning, complete fault memory, and BMW ISTA test plan. If the VIN and production date match a BMW action, follow that bulletin: inspect the specified sensor-link holders, apply the specified software correction, or inspect the affected air line as directed. For other vehicles, test the particular system shown by the VIN and fault path before selecting any component. Do not buy a compressor, strut, spring, or conversion kit until the failed part and its VIN-specific number are established. This article intentionally has no retail link because no single part repairs all of these conditions.",
