      "title": "E70 Rear Air-Supply Unit: Diagnose the Self-Leveling System First",
      "description": "An E70 X5 equipped with rear self-leveling suspension can sit low, lean, run the air supply repeatedly, or display a suspension warning when the electronic ride-height system cannot reach its target. The air-supply unit can fail, but the same symptoms can come from a leaking air spring or line, valve block, ride-height sensor or linkage, wiring, fuse/relay, low voltage, or control/calibration fault. BMW part 37-20-6-859-714 is the current complete replacement air-supply system for the E70 application and supersedes the previously published 37-20-6-789-938; it is not a universal F15 or G05 X5 part.",
      "solution": "Read the EHC fault memory and run the applicable BMW ISTA test plan before ordering a compressor. Confirm the vehicle is equipped with rear self-leveling suspension, compare left/right ride height, check system power and wiring, inspect the height-sensor links, and leak-test the air springs, lines, and valve system. Test the air supply only after those checks isolate it. If BMW ETK/AIR selects the E70 air-supply system for the VIN and diagnosis confirms that assembly, replace it with current part 37-20-6-859-714, follow the BMW repair procedure, clear faults, and perform the required ride-height calibration. Do not install a generic compressor or a coil-conversion kit from symptoms alone.",
